{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 10,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Israel ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an empty vine, he bringeth forth fruit to himself: according to the multitude of his fruit he hath multiplied the altars; according to the goodness of his land they have made goodly images.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Their heart is divided; now shall they be found faulty: he shall break down their altars, he shall spoil their images.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For now they shall say, We have no king, because we feared not the LORD; what then should a king do to us?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They have spoken words, swearing falsely in making a covenant: thus judgment springeth up as hemlock in the furrows of the field.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The inhabitants of Samaria shall fear because of the calves of Beth-aven: for its people shall mourn over it, and its priests ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rejoiced on it, for its glory, because it is departed from it.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It shall also be carried to Assyria, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a present to king Jareb: Ephraim shall receive shame, and Israel shall be ashamed of his own counsel.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Samaria, her king is cut off as the foam upon the water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The high places also of Aven, the sin of Israel, shall be destroyed: the thorn and the thistle shall come up on their altars; and they shall say to the mountains, Cover us; and to the hills, Fall on us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Israel, thou hast sinned from the days of Gibeah: there they stood: the battle in Gibeah against the children of iniquity did not overtake them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in my desire that I should chastise them; and the people shall be gathered against them, when they shall bind themselves in their two furrows.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And Ephraim ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a heifer ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " taught, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " loveth to tread out ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the corn",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; but I passed over upon her fair neck: I will make Ephraim to ride; Judah shall plow, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jacob shall break his clods.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sow to yourselves in righteousness, reap in mercy; break up your fallow ground: for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " time to seek the LORD, till he shall come and reign righteousness upon you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye have plowed wickedness, ye have reaped iniquity; ye have eaten the fruit of lies: because thou hast trusted in thy way, in the multitude of thy mighty men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore shall a tumult arise among thy people, and all thy fortresses shall be plundered, as Shalman plundered Beth-arbel in the day of battle: the mother was dashed in pieces upon ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "her",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.10.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.10.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So shall Beth-el do to you because of your great wickedness: in a morning shall the king of Israel be utterly cut off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
